  triage:description "The sync crate retains a direct normal dependency on sc-observability-types, but ADR-SYNC-0006 as amended by ADR-SYNC-0008:662–674 does not authorize it, and the current allowed third-party Crate Layout row (docs/architecture.md:152) also omits it. The genuine public sc_cron::observability facade now provides every canonical type used by cron_log.rs; a full sync-crate source/manifest sweep finds no remaining use of sc-observability-types outside this declaration. The exact prerelease source amendment authorizes the scheduler/command source pair and retains existing structural restrictions; it does not add this separate direct dependency. A passing workspace-edge/isolated graph check does not amend the exhaustive dependency contract." ;
  triage:remediation "Remove the unused sc-observability-types normal dependency from bd-cache-sync and let Cargo update the sync package dependency list in Cargo.lock. Keep the workspace entry and legitimate CLI/upstream uses. Preserve the genuine sc_cron::observability receiver, exact qualified pin and all current graph restrictions; qualify the resulting consumer graphs under the ordinary affected checks. No new waiver, approval ceremony or broad dependency amendment is needed." ;
